"""BRAINIAC's brain, the level's boss, which COLLECTOR brings too (sheet 5: ten 2x2 sprites laid out as one 96 x 84
picture: 196 198 200 over 233 235 237 239 over 272 274 276; top-layer enemies 630-639, one frame each, none animated,
no damaged looks (dgr 0), armour 255), polished (2026-10-22, round 37; it replaces wave3_l_parts.py's brain, an
inflated outline banded by the shades with nerves inflated from their pixels, 17.9 pixels high).

Where it appears: BRAINIAC t7000 (event 7, the top layer, link 254: 196 198 200 at x 180 204 228 and dat5 -56, 233 235
237 239 at x 168 192 216 240 and -28, 272 274 276 at 180 204 228 and 0: the middle row 12 pixels further left, as the
sheet lays it out) and COLLECTOR t5700 (episode 6's composer brings BRAINIAC's boss whole; 272 and 274 there are
enemies 1660 and 1661, the same sprites with other guns). No other enemy shows these sprites, none is another sprite's
pixels mirrored, turned or in other ramps. From t7050 its pieces launch (event 31, every 100 ticks) 640 (5 19, a small
red ember: polish_red_ember.py's) and 644 (5 278, polish_lava_star's).

As the sprites and their 4x upscales draw it (the picture's columns and rows; lit from the upper left; ramp 4's
fleshy reds, 0x40 and 0x01 its darkest): a brain seen from above, two hemispheres (columns 9-86 of rows 3-62) parted by
the deep fissure down the middle (columns 47-49, from row 13), folded into gyri (the lit ridges, shades 7-f) between
dark sulci (0x40, 0x41); the frontal lobes rounded at the top, notched at the fissure (rows 3-12); the lower part
darker (rows 45-62, the brain curving away underneath); under it a dark base (rows 60-66) with two blue glands side by
side (ramp 3, columns 40-57 of rows 64-73, lit on their upper left); and nerves hanging below in three loops (rows
66-82: a loop on the left, columns 23-36, one on the right, 59-73, and one round the glands' stalk in the middle,
37-58), thin strands with dark rims.

Built for the game's camera as polish_skull_chest.py and polish_green_shell.py are (one heightfield in the picture's
plane, sheared along the camera's line of sight, y - z tan 20, on polish_gyges_wall.Plate's grid, 0.5 pixel apart,
whose lines are the sprites' edges, so each piece is the cells of its sprite's box and every point is where the
sprite draws it): each hemisphere a dome over its half of the outline (DOME: its height, how far in it rises), the two
parted by the fissure's own dark pixels (FISSURE: each dome rises from them as from the outline), the lower part
curving away (LOWER), the outline's last pixel falling to the layer (EDGE); the gyri as relief from the sprite's fine
shading (GYRI) and the sulci, its darkest pixels, creased (CREASE); the glands domes (GLANDS) glowing a little in their
own blue (a dome reads dark from the slanted camera); the nerves round strands over their pixels (NERVE). Painted by
the sprites' shades (polish_nose_drip_face's Paint, polish_green_shell's way: each face the shade of the pixels under
it, blurred, lifted and lighter where the game's sun lights it less), the sulci and the outline dark (0x40). Heights:
0 to 13.8 (z over the layer: the pieces stand on it, origin; the old brain reached 17.9).

Coordinates as in tyrkit: 1 unit = 1 game pixel, +X right, +Y up the screen, +Z towards the camera; the picture's
middle (its pixel edge 48, 42) is the origin: column c's left edge is x = c - 48, row r's top edge y = 42 - r; a piece
whose sprite's top left pixel is (c0, r0) has its origin at (c0 + 12 - 48, 28 - r0) (models.cfg origin).

models.cfg: the model and sprite lines of brain_top_l ... brain_bot_r stay as they are (origin, yaw=0).

Replaces wave3_l_parts.py's brain (BRAIN, BRAIN_PIECES, build_brain(), brain_piece(), their PIECES entries and the
w.whole("brain", ...) registration) and wave3_l_art.py's BRAIN.

Options after "--": --outdir <dir> (default assets/models/enemies), --check <sheets dir> (the outline as the camera
sees it against the sprites' pixels, the whole and each piece), --preview <prefix>, --only <name,...>.
"""
import os
import sys

import numpy as np

HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(HERE, "..", ".."))
sys.path.insert(0, HERE)
import tyrkit as k  # noqa: E402
import polish_machine_kit as mk  # noqa: E402
import polish_gyges_wall as gw  # noqa: E402  (Plate, the shear to the camera, the faces' light)
from polish_green_shell import edt  # noqa: E402
from polish_nose_drip_face import (S, Ink, Paint, Picture, coverage_check, dome, export_pieces, rounded,  # noqa: E402
                                   smoothstep)

W, H = 96, 84
LAYOUT = [("brain_top_l", 196, 12, 0), ("brain_top_m", 198, 36, 0), ("brain_top_r", 200, 60, 0),
          ("brain_mid_1", 233, 0, 28), ("brain_mid_2", 235, 24, 28), ("brain_mid_3", 237, 48, 28),
          ("brain_mid_4", 239, 72, 28), ("brain_bot_l", 272, 12, 56), ("brain_bot_m", 274, 36, 56),
          ("brain_bot_r", 276, 60, 56)]

DOME = (12.5, 15.0)              # the hemispheres' height and how far in from their outline they rise to it
FISSURE = (45, 52, 8, 64)        # the fissure: its dark pixels in these columns and rows part the hemispheres (each
#                                  dome rises from them as from the outline)
GYRI = (0.42, 1.3)               # the fine shading as relief: per shade, its limit (pixels)
CREASE = 2.0                     # the sulci (the darkest pixels inside) creased this deep (on the full height)
LOWER = (44.0, 64.0, 0.7)        # the lower part (rows) curving away underneath: its height down to this fraction
EDGE = 1.2                       # the outline's last pixel falls to the layer over this (low walls round it)
GLANDS = [((44.0, 68.6), (4.7, 4.9), 4.6), ((52.6, 68.4), (4.6, 4.8), 4.4)]   # middle (column, row), radii, height
GLAND_ROWS = (63, 75)
NERVE_ROWS = 69                  # the nerves: the pixels below this row (but the glands; the dark band over them,
#                                  rows 62-68, is the brain's underside, where they hang from)
NERVE = (1.3, 1.9, 1.3)          # their strands' foot height, rise, and the half-width they rise over


class Brain:
    """The brain's heightfield in the picture's plane, from the sprites' pixels, on the fine grid (S cells a pixel)."""

    def __init__(self):
        pic = self.pic = Picture(BRAIN, W, H, 3)
        a = pic.a
        body = a >= 0
        rows = np.arange(H)[:, None] + np.zeros((1, W), int)
        cols = np.arange(W)[None, :] + np.zeros((H, 1), int)
        gland_zone = (cols >= 38) & (cols < 60) & (rows >= GLAND_ROWS[0]) & (rows < GLAND_ROWS[1])
        self.gland_pixels = pic.ramp == 3
        mass = body & (rows < NERVE_ROWS) & ~gland_zone
        glands = body & gland_zone
        nerves = body & ~mass & ~glands
        dark = (a == 0x40) | (a == 0x01)
        self.dark = dark
        X, Y = pic.fine_xy()
        frow = pic.top - Y                                    # the fine cells' rows (pixel units)
        fine_body = pic.soft_mask(body)
        fine_mass = pic.soft_mask(mass, 1.0) & fine_body
        fine_glands = pic.soft_mask(glands, 0.6) & fine_body & ~fine_mass
        fine_nerves = pic.soft_mask(nerves, 0.5) & fine_body & ~fine_mass & ~fine_glands
        # The hemispheres: domes over the outline, parted by the fissure's valley.
        c0, c1, r0, r1 = FISSURE
        fissure = dark & (cols >= c0) & (cols < c1) & (rows >= r0) & (rows < r1)
        d_out = edt(fine_mass, 1.0 / S)
        d = edt(fine_mass & ~pic.soft_mask(fissure, 0.5), 1.0 / S)
        z = rounded(d, DOME[0], DOME[1]) * smoothstep(0.0, EDGE, d_out) ** 0.5
        z = z * (1.0 - (1.0 - LOWER[2]) * smoothstep(LOWER[0], LOWER[1], frow))
        # The gyri and sulci from the sprite's shading.
        known = body & ~dark & (pic.ramp == 4) & (a != 0x41)
        soft = gw.blur(gw.fill(pic.shade, known), 0.6)
        broad = gw.blur(gw.fill(pic.shade, known), 2.4)
        fine_rel = pic.coarse(soft - broad)(X, Y)
        z = z + np.clip(GYRI[0] * fine_rel, -GYRI[1], GYRI[1]) * smoothstep(0.5, 3.0, z)
        p = np.pad(body, 1)
        surrounded = np.ones_like(body)
        for dr, dc in ((-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)):
            surrounded &= p[1 + dr:1 + dr + H, 1 + dc:1 + dc + W]
        crease = pic.coarse(gw.blur((dark & surrounded & mass).astype(float), 0.5))(X, Y)
        z = z - CREASE * np.clip(crease, 0.0, 1.0) * np.clip(z / 6.0, 0.0, 1.0)
        z_mass = np.maximum(z, 0.3)
        # The glands: domes on the dark base between them.
        zg = np.full(X.shape, 1.2)
        for (c, r), radii, h in GLANDS:
            zg = np.maximum(zg, 1.0 + dome(X, Y, (pic.x(c), pic.y(r)), radii, h, power=0.55))
        zg = np.minimum(zg, rounded(edt(fine_glands | fine_mass, 1.0 / S), 9.0, 1.2))
        # The nerves: round strands over their pixels.
        e_n = edt(fine_nerves, 1.0 / S)
        zn = NERVE[0] + NERVE[1] * np.sqrt(1.0 - (1.0 - np.clip(e_n / NERVE[2], 0.0, 1.0)) ** 2)
        Z = np.where(fine_mass, z_mass, np.where(fine_glands, zg, np.where(fine_nerves, zn, 0.0)))
        self.inside_fine = fine_mass | fine_glands | fine_nerves
        self.field = pic.fine(Z)
        self.inside = pic.fine(self.inside_fine.astype(float))
        self.glands = pic.fine(fine_glands.astype(float))

    def heights(self, X, Y):
        return self.field(X, Y)

    def cells(self, X, Y):
        return self.inside(X, Y) > 0.5


GLAND_GLOWS = {0x35: 0.14, 0x37: 0.18, 0x39: 0.22, 0x3b: 0.26}
INKS = lambda pic: [   # noqa: E731
    Ink("flesh", (pic.ramp == 4) & (pic.a >= 0x41), [0x42, 0x43, 0x44, 0x45, 0x46, 0x47, 0x48, 0x49, 0x4a, 0x4b, 0x4d],
        (0.08, 0.4), lift=1.0, comp=1.4),
    Ink("gland", pic.ramp == 3, [0x35, 0x37, 0x39, 0x3b], (0.1, 0.18), lift=1.0, comp=1.0, glows=GLAND_GLOWS,
        sigma=0.6),
]
DARK = 0x40


def build():
    options = k.args()
    out = mk.outdir(options)
    only = set(options["only"].split(",")) if "only" in options else None
    brain = Brain()
    pic = brain.pic
    if "check" in options and only is None:
        sheets = options["check"]
        coverage_check("the brain (its 96 x 84 picture)", pic, brain.cells, LAYOUT,
                       os.path.join(sheets, "enemy_5.png") if os.path.isdir(sheets) else sheets)
    plate = gw.Plate((pic.left, -pic.left, -pic.top, pic.top), brain.heights, cells=brain.cells)
    paint = Paint(pic, INKS(pic), brain.dark, "brain", DARK)

    def paint_faces(obj, kinds, wall_z):
        centres, normals = gw.face_data(obj)
        centres, normals = np.round(centres, 4), np.round(normals, 4)
        on_gland = brain.glands(centres[:, 0], centres[:, 1]) > 0.5
        gland = gw.blur(brain.gland_pixels.astype(float), 0.6)
        near = pic.coarse(gland)(centres[:, 0], centres[:, 1]) > 0.3
        force = ["gland" if g and n else None for g, n in zip(on_gland, near)]
        top = paint.keys(centres[:, 0], centres[:, 1], normals, force=force)
        paint.assign(obj, [top[i] if kinds[i] == 0 else "dark" for i in range(len(kinds))])
    export_pieces(pic, plate, LAYOUT, paint_faces, out, options, only)


